// blaze, the trailer: exactly 60 seconds at 60 fps for X, landscape and upright from one scene. One flight: the
// camera moves through a dark sea of points, and each idea is a landmark of light it nears, holds on and flies through
// (harness-video's src/backdrop.rs), with one caption at a time under it, each still for at least a second and a half.
// Eleven shots, cut to a score in A minor at 88 (src/music.rs: one motif, introduced, built, dropped and answered);
// every cut is on a bar line. Every number is a row of data.json beside this file.
//
//   cd crates/harness
//   harness-video score DIR                                                                # the score, stems, page, pictures
//   cp DIR/music-temp-score.wav harness-video/scene/blaze/music.wav                        # (or the owner's track)
//   harness-video analyse harness-video/scene/blaze/music.wav harness-video/scene/blaze/beats.json
//   harness-video harness-video/scene/blaze/film.flecs film.mp4 x-landscape-1080p60        # the film, read back
//   harness-video harness-video/scene/blaze/film.flecs film-tall.mp4 x-portrait-1080x1920  # the same, upright
//   harness-video harness-video/scene/blaze/film.flecs cuts                                # every cut, on the grid
//   harness-video harness-video/scene/blaze/film.flecs sheet.png contact 0.5               # a frame each half second
//
// Storyboard (cuts.flecs has the positions; times are with our score). Each shot: bars, its landmark, its caption,
// what in the tree backs it, and the sentence a first-time viewer should be able to say back.
//
//   bars   at     shot      landmark                    caption                           backed by / says back
//   1-2    0.00   cage      a hexagon nothing leaves    "build.rs: no network"            AGENTS.md rule 9; the sandbox refuses a script's
//                                                                                         network / "build scripts are locked in"
//   3      5.45   unclosed  INTERRUPT (accent field)    "unclosed file: compile error"    crates/blaze-std/src/fs.rs:1287 (linear File);
//                                                                                         hir-ty-linear / "forgetting to close is an error"
//   4      8.18   name      the sea; the galaxy, far    "blaze", "a compiler for agents"  AGENTS.md / "it is called blaze, for agents"
//   5-6    10.91  rings     arcs that only narrow       "nothing ambient", then           crates/blaze-std/src/lib.rs:10-12 / "you get
//                                                       "capabilities only narrow"        handed access, and it only shrinks"
//   7-8    16.36  disk      a disk tears, time runs     "same code, fake disk", then      crates/blaze-core/src/sim.rs / "it runs on a
//                           back, it tears again        "the bug replays"                 simulated disk and the failure repeats exactly"
//   9-10   21.82  tree      a proof tree closing        "90 theorems, in Lean"            lean/theorems.json / "parts are proved"
//   11-12  27.27  ripples   three rings to one shore    "no-op run", three names, times   data.json rows.noop / "blaze's run is fastest
//                                                                                         of the three, 11.9 ms"
//   13-14  32.73  near      the galaxy nears, is still  (none)                            / "something big is coming"
//   15-18  38.18  galaxy    THE PEAK, on the drop:      "one edit", then                  docs/v2/plan/design/code-identity.md; rule 52 /
//                           dive, edit, four readers    "nothing compiled twice"          "one change touches one function"
//   19-20  49.09  hub       a comb lit from the middle  "soon", "a hub, no checkout"      SOON: branch hub-1111 / "a hub is coming"
//   21-22  54.55  end       the sea streams in          the mark, the repository          / "blaze, on GitHub"
//
// The open loop: the galaxy is in the sky behind the name; the film arrives in it on the drop.
// Honesty: a claim on screen is something the tree has, or is under the "soon" tag. The one comparison is a measured
// row, drawn to scale (each ring's time to the shore is its share of the slowest's), its conditions passing once.
// Sound: the score, with a few of the shots' own sounds under it (`harness-video ... sounds` lists them).
include cuts
include tokens
include parts
include cage
include unclosed
include name
include rings
include disk
include tree
include ripples
include near
include galaxy
include hub
include end

@tree ChildOf
film : ui.ZStack {
  Video: {width: 960, height: 540, fps: 60, seconds: $t_out, scale: 2, reframes: true}
  // The picture: which landmark and its numbers are cued by each beat.
  Backdrop: {shot: 0, at: 0, a: 0, b: 0, c: 0, d: 0, e: 0, f: 1}
  // -16 LUFS integrated, no true peak over -1 dBTP: loud enough on a phone, with headroom for X's re-encode.
  Mix: {lufs: -16, peak: -1}
  Flex: {axis: Z, gap: 0, align: Center, justify: Center, wrap: false}
  Size: {w: {kind: Fixed, value: 960, min: 0, max: 0}, h: {kind: Fixed, value: 540, min: 0, max: 0}}
  // The film is cut to a track: music.wav beside this file (not in the tree: the owner's file, or the temp score
  // `harness-video score` writes), its grid in beats.json. The beats' own sounds sit under it.
  Music: {gain: 1.0, under: 0.4}
}
